## 3. QEMU Plugin Command Line Assembly

**File:** `/home/nick/work/andesim/qemu_plugin/hybrid_handoff.c` lines 537-599 (`qemu_plugin_install()`)

Plugin args are parsed as key=value pairs:

```c
QEMU_PLUGIN_EXPORT int qemu_plugin_install(qemu_plugin_id_t id,
                                           const qemu_info_t *info,
                                           int argc, char **argv)
{
    for (int i = 0; i < argc; i++) {
        g_auto(GStrv) tok = g_strsplit(argv[i], "=", 2);
        if (g_strcmp0(tok[0], "outfile") == 0 && tok[1]) {
            outfile_path = g_strdup(tok[1]);
        } else if (g_strcmp0(tok[0], "enter_pc") == 0 && tok[1]) {
            enter_pc_arg = (uint64_t) v;
            pc_mode = 1;
        } else if (g_strcmp0(tok[0], "exit_pc") == 0 && tok[1]) {
            exit_pc_arg = (uint64_t) v;
            exit_pc_mode = 1;
        } else if (g_strcmp0(tok[0], "exit_marker") == 0 && tok[1]) {
            exit_marker_mode = (v != 0);
        } else if (g_strcmp0(tok[0], "drain_pc") == 0 && tok[1]) {
            drain_pc_arg = (uint64_t) v;
            drain_pc_set = 1;
        }
    }
    if (!outfile_path) {
        fputs("hybrid_handoff: outfile=PATH is required\n", stderr);
        return -1;
    }
}
```

**Supported plugin arguments:**
- `outfile=PATH` (required): state file output path
- `enter_pc=0x...` (optional): PC-mode entry boundary
- `exit_pc=0x...` (optional, verify-oracle): exit PC for pure-QEMU oracle drain
- `exit_marker=1` (optional, verify-oracle): exit on marker
- `drain_pc=0x...` (optional, verify-oracle): drain at this specific PC

The plugin arg assembly happens in `/home/nick/work/andesim/driver/run_plan.cpp` lines 58-109 (`leg_trigger_args()` function), which builds the `,`-suffix appended to the `-plugin` token.

