## 4. Engine-Specific CSR Filtering for `--verify`

**File:** `/home/nick/work/andesim/driver/state_diff.cpp` lines 111-131

```cpp
auto andes_supported_csr = [&](std::string_view name) {
    if (andes_supported.empty()) return true;  // empty list = compare all
    for (const std::string& s : andes_supported)
      if (s == name) return true;
    return false;
  };

if (ref.flags & HYBRID_FLAG_ANDES) {
#define X(field, addr, name)                                  \
  if (!andes_verify_excluded(name) && andes_supported_csr(name)) \
    cmp(r, name, ref.andes.field, got.andes.field);
    HYBRID_ANDES_CSR_LIST(X)
#undef X
```

The `andes_supported` list (from engine descriptor's `andes_csrs` field) **gates which Andes CSRs are compared**. CSRs not in the list are skipped (line 112-115: empty list => compare all; else check membership). The same filtering applies to M-ext CSRs (lines 136-142) and PMA block (lines 123-130).

